# Environment — NEVER commit .env files with real secrets
# `.env.*` is broadly ignored; the `!`-prefixed lines un-ignore the files that
# are explicitly meant to be committed (generic templates and shared dev
# defaults). Anything matching `.env.stage` / `.env.prod` / `.env` stays out.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.dev
!.env.prod.template

